00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:35.660
from phishing website attacks.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.330
One of those main
tools companies can use

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.670
is Safe Browsing
through Chrome browser.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.830
Google is constantly
scanning the web

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.500
and identifying malicious
phishing websites.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.110
These phishing websites are
then stored in a blacklist

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.550
on Google's servers.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:52.370
This blacklist then gets
synced with Chrome browser.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:55.360
So when an employee opens a
malicious phishing website,

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.380
the website is
automatically blocked

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.850
and the user sees this warning.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:02:59.600
YUFENG GUO: Great.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.360
So even if an employee opens
up one of these websites,

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.350
Chrome can detect it and
alert them before they open up

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:06.260
the website.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.460
LORENA CROWLEY: Exactly.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.170
Chrome browser stops
these employees

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.360
from accidentally
putting sensitive data

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.160
into the hands of attackers.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.560
YUFENG GUO: That's really great.

